## 3. Problems Encountered & Fixed

| # | Problem | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `passlib`'s bcrypt backend threw `AttributeError: module 'bcrypt' has no attribute '__about__'` — a known compatibility break between `passlib` and newer `bcrypt` versions | Removed `passlib` entirely; rewrote `hash_password`/`verify_password` in `auth.py` to call the `bcrypt` library directly, sidestepping the broken version-detection code |
| 2 | Registering with an email that was already used (from an earlier failed attempt) returned `400 Bad Request` | Expected behavior — confirmed the duplicate-email check works correctly; resolved by testing with a fresh email |
| 3 | Wrong virtual environment activated multiple times (a stray `.venv` folder one level above the project) caused `ModuleNotFoundError` for packages that were actually installed correctly elsewhere | Standardized on activating `backend\venv` specifically; confirmed via `pip list` before running the server |

> The `passlib`/`bcrypt` issue is a real, currently-known compatibility problem in the Python ecosystem (not a mistake in the original code) — worth mentioning in the report's challenges section, since working around broken third-party dependencies is a genuine part of backend development.

